      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Firestore as the specific managed NoSQL document store for this Python file. This selection will be clearly reflected in the `query_documents.py` code, ensuring a concrete external provider is identifiable. Now, I'm ready to begin fleshing out the specific implementation details, building the queries.\n\n\n**Specifying the Code**\n\nNow, I'm honing in on the exact structure of `query_documents.py`. The plan is coming together: a function within the file will handle the Firestore queries, incorporating the necessary provider-specific imports and client initialization. This function is the cornerstone of fetching documents.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867937454,
          "start": 1789867935158
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc7145b6001mOOqNuf5YSIdNo",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc7140e4001IeykGElC98ivH1",
