      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Data Store**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up the groundwork for `fetch_document.py`. I'm going with Amazon DynamoDB as the managed NoSQL store; that's the established choice here. I'm making sure it's clearly referenced in the code.\n\n\n**Establishing the Functionality**\n\nI'm now implementing the `fetch_document` function within `fetch_document.py`. I'm leveraging `boto3` to interact with DynamoDB, and I'll include the provider-specific identifiers to make the connection and interactions explicit.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867932893,
          "start": 1789867931381
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc7136f5001qpY5sT57DZ2cee",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc7131f3001uyuMfdSr31rsFC",
      "session_id": "ses_f438ece1cffeXBwjmLH7ML7CwK",
